usage: android_cloud_qa.py [-h] --apk APK --output OUTPUT [--adb ADB]
                           [--serial SERIAL]
                           [--expected-sha256 EXPECTED_SHA256]
                           [--readiness-timeout READINESS_TIMEOUT]
                           [--install-timeout INSTALL_TIMEOUT]
                           [--data-timeout DATA_TIMEOUT]
                           [--engine-timeout ENGINE_TIMEOUT]
                           [--selftest-timeout SELFTEST_TIMEOUT]

Check an existing disposable Android runner against one pinned KaM APK. Does
not boot/stop an emulator or provision a cloud device. Clears only KaM app
data on the selected test device. Success means AUTOMATED_CONTENT_SMOKE_PASS;
menu/controls/gameplay still require review. All ADB work is inside main().

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --apk APK
  --output OUTPUT       New evidence directory; must not exist
  --adb ADB             ADB executable; default: adb from PATH
  --serial SERIAL       Explicit ADB serial; otherwise exactly one device is
                        required
  --expected-sha256 EXPECTED_SHA256
                        Expected APK SHA256, pinned to the workflow artifact
  --readiness-timeout READINESS_TIMEOUT
  --install-timeout INSTALL_TIMEOUT
  --data-timeout DATA_TIMEOUT
  --engine-timeout ENGINE_TIMEOUT
  --selftest-timeout SELFTEST_TIMEOUT
